      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=- 2 x^{2} - 2 x - 2$ at $\\left(-1,-2\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $y=ax+b$.\n\n$a=$ {{slope}}\n\n$b=$ {{intercept}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- 2 x^{2} - 2 x - 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=- 4 x - 2\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(-1\\right)=- 4 \\left(-1\\right) - 2=2\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(2\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-2\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{2}\\left(x-\\left(-1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{2}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(-2\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=- \\frac{1}{2}$ and $b=- \\frac{5}{2}$.",
