      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=2 x^{2} + x + 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=4 x + 1\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=4 \\left(2\\right) + 1=9\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(9\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{9}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(12\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{9}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{9}+\\left(\\frac{2}{9}\\right)+\\left(12\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{110}{9} - \\frac{x}{9}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus $a=- \\frac{1}{9}$ and $b=\\frac{110}{9}$.",
